---
import CaseStudy from '../../components/case-study/CaseStudy.astro';
import Section from '../../components/case-study/Section.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/case-study/Prose.astro';
import Gallery from '../../components/case-study/Gallery.astro';
import Brand from '../../components/case-study/Brand.astro';
import Glyseric from '../../assets/work/specimens/manifesto-glyseric.svg';

import hero from '../../assets/work/manifesto/hero.webp';
import original from '../../assets/work/manifesto/original.webp';
import collage from '../../assets/work/manifesto/collage.webp';
import landing from '../../assets/work/manifesto/landing.webp';
import hackerManifesto from '../../assets/work/manifesto/hacker-manifesto.webp';
import hackerManifestoMobile from '../../assets/work/manifesto/hacker-manifesto-mobile.webp';
import hook from '../../assets/work/manifesto/hook.webp';
import hookVideo from '../../assets/work/manifesto/hook.mp4';
import footer from '../../assets/work/manifesto/footer.webp';
import manifestoPage from '../../assets/work/manifesto/manifesto-page.webp';
import manifestoPage2 from '../../assets/work/manifesto/manifesto-page-2.webp';
import manifestoPage3 from '../../assets/work/manifesto/manifesto-page-3.webp';
import solemn1 from '../../assets/work/manifesto/solemn-1.webp';
import solemn2 from '../../assets/work/manifesto/solemn-2.webp';
import solemn3 from '../../assets/work/manifesto/solemn-3.webp';
import note1 from '../../assets/work/manifesto/note-1.webp';
import note2 from '../../assets/work/manifesto/note-2.webp';
import note3 from '../../assets/work/manifesto/note-3.webp';
---

<CaseStudy
	title="Hack Club’s Manifesto"
	tagline="the Hack Club Gap Year application"
	accent="#ec5750"
	links={[{ label: 'Website', href: 'https://manifesto.hackclub.com' }, { label: 'Github', href: 'https://github.com/hackclub/manifesto' }]}
	hero={hero}
	heroAlt="The Manifesto landing page: a collage of gap year photos beside “hackers wanted.”"
	meta={[
		{ label: 'Role', value: ['Sole Designer & Web Developer'] },
		{ label: 'Shipped', value: ['March 2026'] },
	]}
	fonts="family=Young+Serif"
>
	<Section heading="Problem">
		<Prose>
			<p>
				My manager DM’ed one day and asked me for design advice. He was working on the hiring page.{' '}
				<strong>It was not good.</strong>
			</p>
		</Prose>
		<Gallery
			size="column"
			rows={[[{ src: original, alt: 'A plain, article-style draft of the hiring page' }]]}
			caption="I don’t have the screenshot of the original design, but it it was very similar to a Medium article in terms of format."
		/>
		<Prose>
			<p>
				I told him that I didn’t think anyone would apply. It felt like a blank page with a blob of
				text, and not something that would resonate with people. Would people understand that this
				wasn’t a traditional experience? That this could be impactful?
			</p>
			<p>
				After pointing my grievances with the design, he realized a lot more was needed. I told him
				I had an inkling of a vision, and I could take a crack at designing it.
			</p>
			<p class="cs-pull">He told me that I had 2 days.</p>
		</Prose>
	</Section>

	<Section heading="Exploration">
		<Prose>
			<p>
				The Hack Club Gap Year program is an experience that I have a lot of trouble describing in
				words. I also just didn’t have the time to figure out the best way to communicate it.
			</p>
			<p>This is what prompted the direction of a photo collage.</p>
		</Prose>
		<Gallery
			caption="This collage is a sampling of my albums, the albums of my co-workers and friends, and the shared company album with photos from events that we were responsible for."
			rows={[[{ src: collage, alt: 'A collage of photos from the gap year', aspect: 2780 / 1788 }]]}
		/>
		<Prose>
			<p>
				These are snapshots in different moments all 20 of us went through in our year. <strong>This is how we would remember our year.</strong> (I teared up a bit when sifting through our photos.)
			</p>
			<p>
				It’s disjointed and incoherent, but I think it adds to the message. The work we do has
				unexpected results and leads to interesting journeys. It’s for everyone, and you can be
				ready to expect anything.
			</p>
			<p class="cs-quiet">It also serves very well in juxtaposing a lot of the more serious messaging, i.e. the hacker manifesto.</p>
		</Prose>
		<Gallery
			caption="The collage served the foundation for the landing."
			rows={[[{ src: landing, alt: 'The Manifesto landing page with the photo collage and “hackers wanted.”' }]]}
		/>
		<Prose>
			<p>
				I covered the emotional component of Hack Club Gap Year program, but I had yet to include
				the philosophy.
			</p>
			<p>We have a previous work, called the Hacker Manifesto, which contained this philosophy.</p>
		</Prose>
		<Gallery
			caption="The original version of the site my manager came up with consisted of just this philosophy."
			rows={[
				[
					{ src: hackerManifesto, alt: 'The original Hacker Manifesto page' },
					{ src: hackerManifestoMobile, alt: 'The Hacker Manifesto on a phone' },
				],
			]}
		/>
		<Prose>
			<p>
				I wanted to hone on this philosophy, especially the start, which sums up our philosophy at
				Hack Club.
			</p>
		</Prose>
		<Gallery
			caption="The first few lines I used as a hook."
			rows={[
				[
					{
						src: hook,
						video: { src: hookVideo, width: 2534, height: 1440 },
						alt: 'The opening lines of the manifesto used as a hook',
					},
				],
			]}
		/>
		<Gallery
			caption="The last line in the manifesto, I used as the footer. It felt like a strong call to action." rows={[[{ src: footer, alt: 'The footer: “Hackers Wanted.”' }]]} />
		<Prose>
			<p>
				The original plan was to have the manifesto front and center, but after revisions and
				working it through my manager, we decided that a more detailed job overview would be better
				for our main page.
			</p>
			<p>So I made the manifesto its own page.</p>
		</Prose>
		<Gallery
			rows={[
				[{ src: manifestoPage, alt: 'The standalone manifesto page' }],
				[
					{ src: manifestoPage2, alt: 'A later section of the manifesto page' },
					{ src: manifestoPage3, alt: 'The end of the manifesto page' },
				],
			]}
		/>
	</Section>

	<Section heading="Solution">
		<Prose>
			<p>
				I wanted the feel of the manifesto site to be serious. The Hack Club Gap Year program should
				be something taken seriously, even in all the whimsy.
			</p>
		</Prose>
		<Brand
			palettes={[
				{
					title: 'Primary Colors',
					colors: [
						{ name: 'Hack Club Red', hex: '#EC5750' },
						{ name: 'I Remember Black', hex: '#1C1C1A', outlined: true },
						{ name: 'Impure White', hex: '#EEEEEE' },
					],
				},
			]}
			specimenColor="#ffffff"
			type={[
				{ role: 'Headings', family: 'Young Serif', text: 'Young Serif', size: 32 },
				{ role: 'Subheadings & Paragraph', svg: Glyseric, label: 'Glyseric' },
			]}
		/>
		<Prose>
			<p>
				I sought a serif that didn’t feel too rigid. I wanted to avoid something that felt too
				impressing on a person. The slight funk and curves of Young Serif and Glyseric nailed a{' '}
				<strong>balance between seriousness and friendliness</strong>.
			</p>
			<p>The imperfect colors also added to lessening the rigidity and seriousness of the application.</p>
		</Prose>
		<Gallery
			caption="The collage layout stayed a consistent motif in certain elements, bringing uniformity."
			size="column"
			rows={[
				[{ src: solemn1, alt: 'A full-bleed manifesto section in Young Serif' }],
				[{ src: solemn2, alt: 'A heavy, large-scale section of the site', aspect: 351.5 / 265.5 }],
				[
					{
						src: solemn3,
						alt: 'The collage motif reused in a later section',
						aspect: 342.12 / 215.28,
						crop: { width: 100, height: 120.04, left: 0.04, top: -0.14 },
					},
				],
			]}
		/>
		<Prose>
			<p>
				Elements on these pages are large and feel heavy when scrolling. The scale doesn’t feel
				overwhelming with the layout, and the heaviness forces the reader to immerse and view
				specific content pieces, rather than skimming through. It also conveys impact.
			</p>
		</Prose>
	</Section>

	<Section heading="Reflection">
		<Prose>
			<p>
				After the 48 hour deadline was up, I found the end result to be satisfying, despite not being
				perfect. <strong>I’m very proud of the manifesto.</strong> It is not my best work, but for the
				short time frame, I made the best choices I thought I could.
			</p>
			<p class="cs-pull">Designing the Manifesto was an emotional exploration for me.</p>
			<p>
				I viewed my gap year as a rich engagement with both my life and philosophy, and I wanted to
				communicate that to prospective applicants.
			</p>
			<p>
				Many people have reached out to me saying how much they appreciate the effort I put into it.
				One of my coworkers made{' '}
				<a href="https://journal.tongyu.fish/gapyear/">a nice little blog</a> inspired by the
				manifesto site.
			</p>
			<p class="cs-quiet">
				However, in the future for short term and rapidly changing work, I need to be ready to build
				flexibility. The collages did not handle well when content changed, and it led to some places
				having awkward spacing.
			</p>
			<p>
				As a fun but caring aside, I hid a{' '}
				<a href="https://manifesto.hackclub.com/a-designers-note">small hidden note</a> in the site an
				hour after it launched.
			</p>
		</Prose>
		<Gallery
			caption="My manager later asked me to make a section with both me & my coworker’s writings. Making a notes own section made both of our work more visible, and a lot more people read it."
			rows={[
				[
					{ src: note1, alt: 'The hidden designer’s note on a phone' },
					{ src: note2, alt: 'The notes section with both writings' },
				],
			]}
		/>
		<Prose>
			<p>
				I had a couple people reach out to me and say <strong>how it much it meant to them</strong>. It was really
				sweet, and I’m grateful that my words had an impact on them.
			</p>
		</Prose>
		<Gallery rows={[[{ src: note3, alt: 'A message from someone who read the note' }]]} />
	</Section>
</CaseStudy>
